Logistic Regression Hyperparameters:

C (Regularization Strength)
Default: 1.0
Range: Positive float (e.g., 0.001 to 100)
What it does: Controls how much to penalize large weights
Smaller C = stronger regularization = simpler model = may underfit
Larger C = weaker regularization = more complex model = may overfit
Try: 0.01, 0.1, 1.0, 10, 100

penalty (Regularization Type)
Default: 'l2'
Options: 'l1', 'l2', 'elasticnet', 'none'
What it does: Type of regularization applied to weights
'l2': Ridge regularization, shrinks all weights proportionally
'l1': Lasso regularization, can set some weights to exactly zero (feature selection)
'elasticnet': Mix of l1 and l2
'none': No regularization
Note: Not all solvers support all penalties

solver (Optimization Algorithm)
Default: 'lbfgs'
Options: 'lbfgs', 'liblinear', 'saga', 'newton-cg', 'sag'
What it does: Algorithm used to find optimal weights
'lbfgs': Good for small datasets, handles multiclass well, supports l2 and none
'liblinear': Good for small datasets, supports l1 and l2, binary/one-vs-rest only
'saga': Good for large datasets, supports all penalties including elasticnet
'newton-cg': Similar to lbfgs, supports l2 and none
'sag': Faster variant of saga but no l1 support
Common combinations:
l2 penalty -> lbfgs or newton-cg
l1 penalty -> liblinear or saga
elasticnet -> saga

class_weight (Class Balancing)
Default: None
Options: None, 'balanced', or dict
What it does: Adjusts for imbalanced classes
None: All classes weighted equally
'balanced': Automatically adjusts weights inversely proportional to class frequencies
dict: Manually specify weight for each class (e.g., {0: 1, 1: 2, 2: 1})
Use 'balanced' when: You have unequal class sizes and want to prevent bias toward majority class

max_iter (Maximum Iterations)
Default: 100 (but we use 1000)
Range: Positive integer
What it does: Maximum number of iterations for the solver to converge
Too low: May not converge, gives warning
Too high: Takes longer but ensures convergence
Typical range: 100 to 10000
If you get convergence warnings, increase this value
